English translation of the original Japanese commit message:

ci: pin Rust 1.98.1 and expand native lint and MSRV gates

Pin Linux, Windows, macOS, N-API, and guard jobs to Rust 1.98.1 to avoid
unexpected gate changes when upstream stable advances. Add
.github/scripts/check-toolchain-pins.py to catch inconsistent pins and
direct cargo/rustc jobs with no declared toolchain. MSRV exemptions use
cargo metadata rust-version values rather than job names. Add a
non-blocking upstream-stable preview for Clippy and tests. Native
Windows/macOS crates get Clippy --all-targets -D warnings. Expand MSRV
gates to nine Rust 1.85 crates and four Rust 1.91 add-ons (ffi, napi,
py, vad). Linux cross-checks the two OS-only crates for compilation;
native jobs cover linking/tests. MSRV jobs omit Clippy because its lints
change by version.
